WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.024
Monitoring understanding means checking comprehension while reading, listening, practicing, or solving a problem.

2
00:00:05.024 --> 00:00:12.367
Instead of waiting until the end to discover that the thread was lost, you notice confusion as it appears.

3
00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:22.801
You pay attention to moments when the details stop connecting, when a term is unclear, when an assumption slips in unnoticed, or when progress is only superficial.

4
00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:27.438
This skill is especially important in complex work because errors can compound.

5
00:00:27.438 --> 00:00:32.462
A small misunderstanding in the first step can shape every decision that follows.

6
00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:37.873
In troubleshooting, a weak assumption can cause a person to collect the wrong evidence.

7
00:00:37.873 --> 00:00:42.897
In writing, an unclear claim can make the rest of the argument unstable.

8
00:00:42.897 --> 00:00:46.761
Monitoring lets you adjust before the cost of correction grows.

9
00:00:46.761 --> 00:00:48.307
Good monitoring uses questions.

10
00:00:48.307 --> 00:00:50.626
What do I think this means?

11
00:00:50.626 --> 00:00:52.558
What evidence supports that interpretation?

12
00:00:52.558 --> 00:00:54.490
Which part is still uncertain?

13
00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.423
What assumption am I making?

14
00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:59.514
Could I explain the last step without looking?

15
00:00:59.514 --> 00:01:03.379
What would I need to see to change my mind?

16
00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:08.403
These questions slow the work just enough to keep it aligned with reality.

17
00:01:08.403 --> 00:01:11.495
Monitoring does not mean stopping every few seconds.

18
00:01:11.495 --> 00:01:14.200
It means creating checkpoints at meaningful moments.

19
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:19.997
Pause after a section, a decision, a failed attempt, or a new piece of evidence.

20
00:01:19.997 --> 00:01:22.702
If the material still makes sense, continue.

21
00:01:22.702 --> 00:01:31.977
If it does not, change the strategy: reread, draw a diagram, ask a better question, test the assumption, or seek review before errors harden.

22
00:01:31.977 --> 00:01:36.228
A useful signal is the phrase, I sort of get it.

23
00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:39.320
That may be true, but it deserves testing.

24
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:46.276
Sort of understanding is often enough to follow someone else's explanation, but not enough to act independently.

25
00:01:46.276 --> 00:01:56.710
When that feeling appears, convert it into a concrete check: summarize the idea, apply it to a small case, or name the part that is still unclear.
